<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anand district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anand is a district of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, formed in 1997 from part of Kheda district, with its headquarters at the town of Anand. The town is famous as the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amol">Amul</a> dairy co-operative, which grew from 1946 into the centre of India's White Revolution. The district includes the old port town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khambhat">Khambhat</a>, formerly Cambay.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anand-district.jpg" alt="Anand district" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Santanu Sen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borsad_stepwell_-_inside_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
